chaddr (1.0.5) testing; urgency=medium

  * Resource type: router — diagnose and apply OpenWrt Shadowsocks remote
    server addresses over SSH/UCI (system: openwrt, config: shadowsocks
    remote server); host defaults to the IPv4 default gateway; password from
    the profile or router_password in chaddr.conf; depends on python3-paramiko
  * Profiles: optional: true (also yes/on/1) on any type block lists it in
    the GUI Instructions tab deselected by default; the CLI still runs it
    unless an instruction filter is applied
  * Documentation and packaging: README, chaddr-profile(5), profile/example,
    chaddr.conf.template, and Debian package description cover router and
    optional instructions

