chaddr (1.0.4) testing; urgency=medium

  * Packaging: fix installed /usr/bin/chaddr ModuleNotFoundError when
    /usr/bin/env python3 resolves to a venv; generate launcher from
    chaddr.py.in with /usr/bin/python3 shebang and embedded PY_INSTALL_DIR,
    and fall back to system dist-packages from the source-tree launcher
  * Public IP: try providers in priority waves (AWS checkip / ipify /
    icanhazip / ident.me first) with a larger fallback set and more robust
    response parsing so status-bar client IP fetch succeeds more often
  * Privilege: in GUI mode prefer pkexec/gksudo/kdesudo over TTY sudo, with
    a wx password dialog feeding sudo -S as fallback for protected writes
  * Profiles: addr-history is one address per line with optional
    YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS timestamps; legacy multi-IP lines still load and are
    migrated on append; expose ordered from/type instruction AST; accept
    changelog: <path> shorthand; show complete registered nameserver host lists
  * Resource type: changelog — bump Debian changelog version on apply and
    record "chaddr IPv4/IPv6 from <old> to <new>", reusing prior dist/author
  * GUI: profile dropdown; Instructions | Addresses notebook (Addresses
    default); session-toggleable instructions filter diagnose/renew/apply;
    sortable Type/Family/Address/Timestamp table with numeric IP and datetime
    sort, ▲/▼ headers, and gray history rows except current resolve
  * GUI: stop freezes from DNS/cloud work on the UI thread before operations;
    de-duplicate spare address sets; Ctrl+PgUp/PgDn for detail tabs;
    Alt+Left/Right for profiles; resolve timestamps; right-click status-bar
    remote IP to copy with notification

