chaddr (1.0.2) testing; urgency=medium

  * Profiles: support multiple from: blocks per profile (resolve, ec2 instance,
    aliyun instance); merge instance ID from from: blocks into elastic-IP
    handlers; append renewed addresses to addr-history in the profile file
  * Profiles: iter_profile_address_fetch and list_profile_candidate_addresses
    collect history, resolve, instance, and old-ip sources; CLI -A/--addresses
    lists candidates with source labels (including instance ID in display)
  * Aliyun Elastic IP: when instance: is set, look up that ECS instance only
    (do not fall back to the first running instance in the region)
  * Resource type: file — plain-text IP literal replace with alnum-boundary
    regex (not \\b); diagnose Apply preview with > prefix lines
  * Apply: verbose orchestration logging (old-address resolution path, spare
    sets, per-handler progress, change counts); profile spare passed to handlers;
    registered nameserver Apply sets ns: glue to selected IPv4 without matching
    profile old IP; file handlers log match candidates and replacement counts
  * GUI: single Addresses panel (multi-select apply, CRUD for manual entries);
    progressive address loading with status-bar progress and stop control;
    Apply/Renew activate the profile Logging tab; reduce STC focus churn when
    appending logs
  * GUI: diagnose activates per-profile log and diagnostics tabs; renew saves
    addr-history after success
  * CLI/GUI: set GTK_A11Y=none on Linux to reduce accessibility warnings
  * Documentation: README, chaddr(1), chaddr-profile(5), bash completion for -A

